# Windows line endings for anything Windows runs.
#
# Without this, Git ships these files with Unix line endings. A .bat with LF
# endings behaves unpredictably when double-clicked on Windows - the August
# package went out that way. Verify after publishing by downloading the zip
# from GitHub and running `file` on a .bat: it must say CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.txt text eol=crlf
*.sql text eol=crlf
